error: `lock` on a file holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_file_lock_async_held.sg:4:14
 4 |     try file.lock()
   |              ^^^^
  hint: `await file.lockAsync()` does the same work without holding the thread
